   backgrounds so its pixels show through. Borders, glows and text
   stay — selection keeps a flat translucent fill instead of the
   gradient wash. Text gets a soft shadow for legibility over video. */
html.glass-native #panel {
  background: transparent;
  box-shadow: none;
  border-radius: 0;
  clip-path: var(--glass-clip);
  /* Subtitle-style legibility: a tight near-opaque shadow carries text
     over any backdrop, the soft one keeps the edge from reading as a
     stroke. The tint alone cannot guarantee contrast — partial
     transmission leaves a mid-luminance surface in bright scenes. */
  text-shadow:
    0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8),
    0 1px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
}

/* Light material (dark text): no halo. The near-black text already
   carries itself on a bright surface, and the dark shadow above reads as
   a smudge under it, while a light one reads as a glow neither wanted.
   The halo is a dark-surface device only. */
html.glass-native.glass-light #panel {
  text-shadow: none;
}

/* Vibrancy: the text follows the material, not the system theme, so a
   bright backdrop hands the panel a light surface with dark text.
   Text, surfaces and hairlines flip together — a half-flipped palette
   would put dark text on a dark menu. Accent and action colours stay:
   they are picked to read on either surface. */
html.glass-native.glass-light {
  --bg: #ffffff;
  --bg-opaque: #ffffff;
  --scrollbar-thumb: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
  --panel-highlight: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.65);
  --panel-edge: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  --panel-glint: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
  --panel-sheen: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  --panel-reflection: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045);
  --panel-bottom-edge: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.24);
  --border: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  --border-strong: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.14);
  --text: #16161a;
  --text-dim: #4b515c;
  --text-faint: #68717e;
  --sel: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
  --sel-border: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
  --hover: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.11);
  --divider: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07);
  --kbd-bg: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
  --kbd-cap-bg: #ffffff;
  --kbd-cap-border: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
  --icon-bg: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
  --text-select: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
}

html.glass-native.glass-dark {
  --bg: #1e1e1e;
  --bg-opaque: #1e1e1e;
  --scrollbar-thumb: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28);
  --panel-highlight: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  --panel-edge: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  --panel-glint: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  --panel-sheen: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  --panel-reflection: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045);
  --panel-bottom-edge: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.24);
  --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);
  --border-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
  --text: #f4f4f6;
  --text-dim: #c3c9d2;
  --text-faint: #aeb6c2;
  --sel: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07);
  --sel-border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  --hover: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  --divider: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  --kbd-bg: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  --kbd-cap-bg: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  --kbd-cap-border: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  --icon-bg: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  --text-select: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28);
}

/* The material flip above is a step change in the palette; ease the
   properties that consume it so a flip reads as a fade rather than a
   flash. Scoped to the swap window (html.glass-fading is armed by the
   page for ~300ms) so it never overrides the hover and selection
   transitions of the base rules. */
html.glass-fading #panel,
html.glass-fading #panel * {
  transition:
    color 260ms ease,
    background-color 260ms ease,
    border-color 260ms ease,
    fill 260ms ease,
    stroke 260ms ease,
    text-shadow 260ms ease;
}

/* The glint colours are declared on the root, so they transition there:
   the panel and its pseudo-element inherit the eased value. */
html.glass-fading {
  transition:
    --panel-glint 260ms ease,
    --panel-reflection 260ms ease;
}

/* Curved lighting, inner shade and fine dither now live in D2D beneath
   the page. No second, stationary specular layer over the text. */
html.glass-native #panel::before,
html.glass-native #panel::after {
  content: none;
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  html.glass-fading, html.glass-fading * { transition: none !important; }
}

html.glass-native #divider {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 16%, transparent);
}

/* ── opaque panel backgrounds (settings → Appearance) ────────── */
/* Solid paint for light rooms where glass washes out; glass layer
   stays parked (see glass_active) so this costs no capture. */
html.bg-black #panel {
  background: #000000;
  box-shadow: none;
}

html.bg-white #panel {
  background: #ffffff;
  box-shadow: none;
}

/* CSS outline fallback for systems where DWM cannot own the opaque edge. */
html.bg-black #panel::after,
html.bg-white #panel::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  border: 1px solid;
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  pointer-events: none;
}

html.bg-black #panel::after {
  border-color: var(--panel-edge);
}

html.bg-white #panel::after {
  border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.16);
}

/* DWM owns the outline when it also owns the opaque window corners. */
html.opaque-dwm-frame.bg-black #panel::after,
html.opaque-dwm-frame.bg-white #panel::after {
  content: none;
}

html.glass-native .row .icon.placeholder {
  background: transparent;
}

#chat-file-picker[hidden],
#chat-file-picker [hidden] {
