Author:     Habeeb <mshabeeburrahman786@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Wed Oct 21 18:55:59 2026 +0530
Commit:     Habeeb <mshabeeburrahman786@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 21 18:55:59 2026 +0530

    perf(glass): faster show, steady frames

    Show no longer forces a 60px pane before the page measures: the window keeps its retained height and the first resize drives both window and glass, so each show rebuilds the lens once instead of twice. The capture worker now waits on the config channel rather than a 10ms timer, so a show wakes it immediately and idle wakeups drop to the 4Hz material poll.

    Statistics readback is double-buffered: copy the 16x16 sample, map the previous frame with DO_NOT_WAIT. Removes a full D3D11 pipeline sync from every presented frame; the material keeps its current values when the readback is not ready. Region writes are deduped per size/scale.

    Audit and remaining work tracked in docs/plans/glass-show-performance.md.

